Here $$F(z) = z\, e^{-z/2}$$ is a model function selected for φ‑structure and exponential suppression; it is exact in $$\phi$$ but is presented as a conjectural form pending a detailed derivation from a QCD‑like effective theory. The expression is exact and free of rounding; its compatibility with standard QCD axion expectations must be checked explicitly.[8][9][10]

### 5.3 Axion–Photon Coupling

Conventional axion models give a photon coupling of the form[8][9][10]
$$
g_{a\gamma\gamma} = \frac{\alpha}{2\pi f_a}\, C_{a\gamma},
$$
where $$C_{a\gamma}$$ encodes anomaly coefficients.

**Ansatz A4 (φ‑modified coupling).**  
ESQET‑UIFT modifies this as
$$
